                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Anchorage AK",
                "headline": "Winter Weather Advisory issued November 11 at 1:08PM AKST until November 12 at 5:00AM AKST by NWS Anchorage AK",
                "description": "* WHAT...Freezing rain and rain falling on cold surfaces expected.\nTotal ice accumulation of a light glaze.\n\n* WHERE...Western Kenai Peninsula.\n\n* WHEN...From 5 PM this afternoon to 5 AM AKST Thursday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Travel could be difficult. Some roads will become slick.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Areas of light rain, possibly mixed with snow,\nwill develop late this afternoon and become more widespread during\nthe evening. Temperatures will hover right around or a few degrees\nabove freezing through this evening. Colder areas, including hills,\nbridges, and overpasses will be the most likely to see freezing\nrain. Rain will then taper off overnight into Thursday morning,\nwith temperatures cooling to freezing or below. Thus, any water on\nroadways will freeze.",
                "instruction": "Slow down and use caution while traveling. For the latest road\nconditions call 5 1 1 or visit 511.alaska.gov.",
                "response": "Execute",
                "note": null,
                "parameters": {
